      "id": "mu-estimate",
      "kind": "engineering_estimate",
      "title": "MapUnite engineering estimates for values manufacturers don't publish",
      "publisher": "MapUnite",
      "rationale": "Idle speed by segment (commuter 1400, cruiser 1100, naked/sport 1500, adventure 1300, CVT scooter 1700 rpm; sd 100-150 rpm). Redline as 1.10x the power-peak speed for commuters, cruisers and scooters and 1.15x for nakeds and sports, rounded to 250 rpm, sd 6 %. Unpublished gearing from the class-default ratio set of the same gear count. Loaded rolling radius as 0.97x the unloaded radius computed from the rear tyre code (sd 1.5 %). Usable battery energy as 0.90x the stated pack energy where the manufacturer doesn't say which it is."
    },
    {
      "id": "cossalter-2006",
      "kind": "reference_book",
      "title": "Motorcycle Dynamics, 2nd edition",
      "citation": "Cossalter, V. (2006). Motorcycle Dynamics (2nd ed.). Lulu.com.",
      "notes": "Drag area CdA of motorcycle + rider spans about 0.18-0.7 m2 depending on type and riding posture; rolling-resistance coefficient of motorcycle tyres on asphalt about 0.01-0.02 depending on pressure and speed."
